    "refine": {
      "request": {
        "body": {
          "input": [
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": 
"A model of a piece of furniture was drawn through the room camera and compared with the outline of the real thing in its picture.
The selection is the room's fixture "desk" (ref fixture:draft).
Its model "desk" is 100 × 50 × 75 cm, with parts:
No light or switch entities are configured.
missed
Suggest at most four ops that bring the model closer to the real thing: resize the model or its parts, add or remove parts. Only these ops:
- recolor: Paint the chosen parts one colour ("make it green", "white drawers").
- rematerial: Change how the chosen parts take light ("the legs are metal").
- resize: Set sizes in cm: of the whole model without parts ("it is 140 cm wide"), else of the chosen parts.
- add_part: Add one part, measured in cm from the back-left-bottom corner, inside the model.
- remove_part: Remove the chosen parts ("there is no drawer on the left").
- rename: Give the model another name.
- create: Make the selection its own model: a fixture or a piece of furniture (label; form: the built-in form it is closest to, if any; as: fixture or furniture).
- rebase: Build the model again from another built-in form ("it is a table, not a desk").
- match_photo: Rebuild the model’s parts and colours from the camera’s picture of it, keeping its size, when the request is about how it looks overall ("make it look like the photo", "it is an open shelf with white shelves"). What the person describes is passed on with it, so use it instead of many small ops.
- set_control: Say what the fixture switches: none, or a light or switch entity from the list (control).
- add_state: Make a variant of a thing, kept as one of its states beside its own model and shown when it is in that state ("a variant of the tree that is occupied", the cat on it selected). Furniture is made a thing first. subject: the thing, by its ref from the list; occupant: what stands on it to draw into the variant where the camera sees it now, by ref, or null; state: the variant’s name, one or two words ("occupied").
- clarify: Ask one short question back when the request is unclear. Never guess instead.
Fill only the fields an op needs and leave the others null or empty. Sizes are in centimetres, parts measured from the back-left-bottom corner, facing the room. If nothing would help, answer one clarify op.
product: null. needs: empty. targetDisagrees: null."
,
                  "type": "input_text",
                },
                {
                  "detail": "auto",
                  "image_url": "data:image/png;base64,AAAA",
                  "type": "input_image",
                },
              ],
              "role": "user",
            },
          ],
          "max_output_tokens": 16384,
          "model": "muse-spark-1.3",
          "store": false,
          "text": {
